// Clue Name :
"P32673457" "Handwritten Note"
// DetailString :
"P2688752672" "This piece of paper contains the last known location for President Marchand."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RecluseOrders 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2464969056" "Notice from Recluse"
// DetailString :
"P3296655496" "The words on the note fade in and out, as if time itself ages them into nothingness:<br><br>'You have been duped by Marchand.  Your ineptitude is disheartening.  You must prove your worth to me before I will allow you to continue, assassin.'<br><br>Below the reprimand is another set of coordinates.  This isn't looking good for you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BossesDead 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4092526342" "Stamp of Approval"
// DetailString :
"P876673909" "As Calamity breathed his last, he said to you:<br><br>'Well done.  You've survived the three fates worse than death.  Your dedication to Lord Recluse is without question.  Take this sash as proof that you have defeated your final challenge.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CalamitySash 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2144202907" "Calamity's Sash"
// DetailString :
"P224889088" "The sash from Calamity's outfit.  Proof that you have survived Lord Recluse's trial."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P540133404" "The Spider Weaves His Web"
// DetailString :
"P1517229838" "As you arrived at Ouroboros and met Mender Tesseract, she insulted you and then told you that she had a major job for you.  Assassinate President Marchand in 1963 so that Lord Recluse could become the new ruler of the Rogue Isles!  She had some sketchy information about the president's (then) current hiding place and you traveled in time to smoke him out and take him down.  <br><br>Things didn't go exactly as planned.  Not only was President Marchand NOT there, but Miss Liberty was waiting for you.  Not only that, but after you defeated her, her daughter, Ms. Liberty, arrived, itching for a fight.  You managed to defeat both of them, but failed to complete your objective.  Confused, you made your way back to Ouroboros."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P275870665" "As you arrived at Ouroboros and met Mender Tesseract, she insulted you and then told you that she had a major job for you.  Assassinate President Marchand in 1963 so that Lord Recluse could become the new ruler of the Rogue Isles!  She had some sketchy information about the president's (then) current hiding place and you traveled in time to smoke him out and take him down.  <br><br>Things didn't go exactly as planned.  Not only was President Marchand NOT there, but Miss Liberty was waiting for you.  Not only that, but after you defeated her, her daughter, Ms. Liberty, arrived, itching for a fight.  You managed to defeat both of them, but failed to complete your objective.  Confused, you made your way back to Ouroboros.  <br><br>Mender Tesseract didn't seem overly surprised by your incomplete objective.  She did point out that Lord Recluse would see it as failure and directed you to prove your dedication to him.  You had no idea what you were in store for, but you showed up anyway.  What you encountered was the three fates worse than death, a gauntlet of survival against Wrath, Misery, and Calamity.  You survived, and restored Recluse's confidence in you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL5-6_FB_Spider_Weaves_His_Web_V_StoryArc 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P881716340" "Newspaper Clipping"
// tDetailString :
"P4072575556" "Had someone told you that you would be traveling back in time to 1963 to assassinate President Marchand so that Lord Recluse could assume power over the Rogue Isles, you would have told them they were nuts.  But that is exactly what you did.  Through trials of misinformation, a mulish contact, and surviving the three fates worse than death, you proved your dedication to Lord Recluse and finally made it to the Marchand Building in St. Martial.  <br><br>There, you took on loyalists utterly dedicated to keeping Marchand in power, from local citizens to his staff to government operatives hired on to ensure his safety.  They were no match for you.  You completed your mission and history has come full circle to ensure Lord Recluse's reign.  <br>For your trouble and effort, you hold in your hand an old and weathered newspaper clipping, the words barely visible on decaying paper.  The headline reads:<br>'President Marchand dead.  Assassin unknown.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RequiemTimeTravelClue02V 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1026469962" "Dear {HeroName}..."
// DetailString :
"P1867470279" "While time traveling into the past, you visit President Marchand's presidential suite and in a file cabniet you find a hand written letter addressed to {HeroName}...<br><br>I have posed many questions for you in many other times, {HeroName}, but perhaps the most important one is this, 'who is Mender Silos?' He claims to be from a future so far in time that his own science would make it impossible. He claims that humanity has been wiped out, but doesn't say who did it. He claims that he is here to help, but who is he really helping? You, of all people, should be able to detect a ruse when you see one.<br><br>I know that you are currently working for Mender Tesseract. Of all the Menders, I believe her to be the most honest in her ways. If not for Silos' agenda and the dreaded Temporal Scaling, I believe she would have enslaved your time and ruled as empress.  Silos claims that she is 'reformed' from her upbringing, but I do not believe it. Her kind was bred to rule, to conquer, to consume. There is no 'high road' along that path. Tesseract is a nightmare given form, a monster with a pretty smile. Pray you never meet her in her own time.<br><br>Don't allow yourself to be fooled, but don't let yourself be discovered either. Play their game for now; learn everything you can about these Menders. It will aid you later. For now, look for my other letters, {HeroName}. I shall see you in the pillar when the time is right."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3113276024" "While I realize you've barely mastered the complex art of clothing yourself in the morning, {VillainName}, I have an important task for you.  Don't gawp, just listen.<br><br>  Operations are in place to elevate Lord Recluse's authority in the Rogue Isles like never before.  In order to accomplish this, there is one minor detail that you will need to take care of.<br><br>Back in 1964, President Marchand was a thorn in Recluse's side that had to be removed.  You will travel back to 1964 and take care of him.  Now, I do not think I need to remind you that discretion is key.   But it's you, so I must.  There can be NO evidence that leads Marchand's demise back to Lord Recluse.  <br><br><color orange>Note: This series of missions is recommended for group play. You're welcome to try it as a solo player, but it'll be tough. Consider yourself warned.>"
// AcceptString :
"P1357370960" "Find Marchand in his hiding place."
// SendOffString :
"P3290509070" "MOVE, bottom-feeder!  Marchand is a slippery little snake.  You need to catch him before he slinks away."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3290798220" "Go to the Safehouse"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2569099516" "You have everything you need, {VillainName}.  Please tell me you don't need me to hold your hand on this.  I'd have to remove it first.  What I'm really trying to say is, stop standing here and go there so that you can get this job done."
// TaskTitle :
"P1602119782" "<color deepskyblue>The Spider Weaves His Web</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2770291627" "<color deepskyblue>Part One</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2330744805" "Marchand was smart to pick caves for a hiding place.  He's slippery; no wonder he's hiding with snakes.  But now that you're here, it looks like his luck just ran out."

